-- title:
--   Theorem 4.1, part 1 (polar form) — the 322 points of Table 2 are vertices of the polar spindle, with their Σ⁺- and Σ-orbits
-- statement:
--   Let $Q^\Delta\subset\mathbb R^5$ be the polar of Santos's prismatoid (the inequalities $\langle r,x\rangle\le1$ for the 48 rows $r$ of Table 1) and let $V$ be the set of the 322 polar points of Table 2: $\pm e_5$ (rows A and L) and, for every type $X\in\{B,B',\dots,K,K'\}$ and sign pattern $\sigma\in\{\pm1\}^4$, the point $\tfrac1{c_0}(\sigma_1c_1,\dots,\sigma_4c_4,c_5)$. Then:
--
--   1. every point of $V$ is a vertex of $Q^\Delta$, and $V$ has exactly $322=2+20\times16$ elements;
--   2. each letter class (types $X$ and $X'$) has 32 elements and is a single $\Sigma^+$-orbit;
--   3. the $\Sigma$-orbit of $e_5$ and of $-e_5$ is $\{e_5,-e_5\}$ (the union A $\cup$ L);
--   4. the $\Sigma$-orbit of every point of the class of $X$ is the union of the classes of $X$ and of its partner, for the pairs
--   $$B\cup K,\quad C\cup J,\quad D\cup I,\quad E\cup H,\quad F\cup G.$$
--
--   Here $\Sigma^+$ is generated by the 32 orthogonal maps of p. 11 and $\Sigma=\Sigma^+\cup\tau\Sigma^+$ with $\tau(x_1,\dots,x_5)=(x_4,x_3,x_1,x_2,-x_5)$. The vertex claim is the facet half of Santos's description of $Q$; with part 2 it gives the 322 vertices of Theorem 1.6.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Polar form of Theorem 4.1(1): a facet $\langle c,x\rangle\le1$ of $Q$ is the vertex $c$ of $Q^\Delta$, and an orthogonal symmetry $g$ of $Q$ acts on facet normals by $g$ again. The clause "A and L are the bases of the prismatoid" holds by construction: A and L are the polar points $\pm e_5$, which `santos_spindle` identifies with the polars of $Q^\pm$. The six $\Sigma$-orbits are stated as items 3–4, which together with item 1 partition $V$ into six orbits.
-- source:
--   Santos, A counterexample to the Hirsch conjecture, arXiv:1006.2814v3, p. 12, Theorem 4.1, part 1 and Table 2; p. 11 (Σ, Σ⁺)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Hirsch_model
import Definitions.Def_Hirsch_walk
import Definitions.Def_SantosHirsch_Counter_Setting

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

namespace SantosHirsch.Counter

/-- Theorem 4.1, part 1 (p. 12), polar form: the 322 points of Table 2 are distinct vertices
of the polar spindle; each letter carries 32 of them forming one `Σ⁺`-orbit; the `Σ`-orbits
are `{e₅, −e₅}` (A ∪ L) and the unions of the paired letters B ∪ K, C ∪ J, D ∪ I, E ∪ H,
F ∪ G. -/
theorem theorem_4_1_part1 :
    santosVertices ⊆ Set.extremePoints ℝ santosSpindle ∧
    santosVertices.ncard = 322 ∧
    (∀ ℓ : Letter, (letterPoints ℓ).ncard = 32) ∧
    (∀ ℓ : Letter, ∀ p ∈ letterPoints ℓ, sigmaPlusOrbit p = letterPoints ℓ) ∧
    sigmaOrbit apexPlus = {apexPlus, apexMinus} ∧
    sigmaOrbit apexMinus = {apexPlus, apexMinus} ∧
    (∀ ℓ : Letter, ∀ p ∈ letterPoints ℓ,
      sigmaOrbit p = letterPoints ℓ ∪ letterPoints (pairedLetter ℓ)) := by sorry

end SantosHirsch.Counter
